Time and Space Complexity

What is Time Complexity?
Time Complexity tells
How the running time of an algorithm grows when the input size increases.
It does NOT tell the exact execution time.
Example
n = 10
Algorithm A = 1 ms

n = 100000

Algorithm A = 500 ms
We study
Growth Rate
instead of milliseconds.

Why Companies Ask Time Complexity?
Because every company wants efficient code.
Suppose
Searching

Algorithm A
O(n)

Algorithm B
O(log n)
For
n = 1,000,000
Linear Search
Needs almost
1,000,000 comparisons
Binary Search
Needs only
≈20 comparisons
Huge difference.

Big O Notation
Represents
Worst Case Complexity
Example
