Mostly interviewers ask only Big-O.

=> Graph: 




 
As the input size increases:
O(1) remains almost flat.
O(log n) increases very slowly.
O(n) grows proportionally.
O(n log n) is slightly larger than linear.
O(n²) becomes much slower.
O(n³) is impractical for large inputs.
O(2ⁿ) and O(n!) become impossible for even moderate input sizes.


